      "fundamental_ambiguity": "A phone accelerometer reading a_p = R_v^p @ (a_vehicle + g_nav) cannot determine whether a steady-state lateral acceleration component is due to: (1) road bank angle (vehicle body roll), (2) cradle mechanical roll in the mount, or (3) centripetal acceleration during a turn. Without an independent measurement of vehicle body attitude (e.g., wheel speed differential, suspension height, or road geometry), R_n^v pitch/roll remain unidentifiable."
